# Talkapo — Supabase connection
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in the two values from
# your Supabase project: Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
#
# Leave them blank and the site still builds and deploys. The Talkapo demo just
# runs read-only on seed content and says so on the page — nothing else in the
# portfolio touches Supabase at all.
#
# Both of these are PUBLIC by design. The anon key identifies the project and
# nothing more; every table it can reach is behind row-level security, defined
# in supabase/migrations/0001_talkapo.sql.
#
# Never add the service_role key here or anywhere else in this repo. It bypasses
# RLS entirely, and `NEXT_PUBLIC_` values are compiled into the browser bundle.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
